questions.solution:
The higher the charge on the metal ion, smaller is the ionic size and more is the complex forming ability. Thus, the degree of complex formation decreases in the order

M^{4+}>M_2^{2+}>M^{3+}>M $\mathrm{O}_{2}^{+}

The higher tendency of complex formation of \mathrm{MO}_2^{2+} as compared to $ M^{3+}$ is due to high concentration of charge on metal atom $M$ in  \mathrm{MO}_{2}^{2+}.$

Change in colour is due to the oxidation of alcohol with potassium dichromate. Oxidation of alcohols with $\mathrm{K}_2 \mathrm{Cr}_2 \mathrm{O}_7$ in dilute $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{SO}_4$ (orange solution):
<img src="https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/aiims/_Cj7jed9BTNiw25IIMRo8IWVAxpb-FeRJFPyBzYP2bM.original.fullsize.png"><br>
$\mathrm{K}_2 \mathrm{Cr}_2 \mathrm{O}_7$ in presence of dilute $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{SO}_4$ acts as an oxidising agent. It is converted into chromic sulphate which is green in colour.
$$
\begin{gathered}
\mathrm{K}_2 \mathrm{Cr}_2 \mathrm{O}_7+4 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{SO}_4 \rightarrow \mathrm{K}_2 \mathrm{SO}_4+\mathrm{Cr}_2\left(\mathrm{SO}_4\right)_3+4 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}+\frac{3}{2} \mathrm{O}_2 \\
\text{ (orange) }
\end{gathered}
$$
(green)

